{"id":"CVE-2018-15919","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2018-08-28T08:00:00.000Z","updated":"2025-12-18T11:48:27.405Z","description":"Remotely observable behaviour in auth-gss2.c in OpenSSH through 7.8 could be used by remote attackers to detect existence of users on a target system when GSS2 is in use. NOTE: the discoverer states 'We understand that the OpenSSH developers do not want to treat such a username enumeration (or \"oracle\") as a vulnerability.'","cwe":["n/a","CWE-200 CWE-200 Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","v":"3.1","score":5.3,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"poc","Automatable":"yes","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20181221-0001/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/105163","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"105163"},{"url":"http://seclists.org/oss-sec/2018/q3/180","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["openssh"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-20685","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2019-01-10T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2025-12-17T21:53:56.287Z","description":"In OpenSSH 7.9, scp.c in the scp client allows remote SSH servers to bypass intended access restrictions via the filename of . or an empty filename. The impact is modifying the permissions of the target directory on the client side.","cwe":["n/a","CWE-863 CWE-863 Incorrect Authorization"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","v":"3.1","score":5.3,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2019/dsa-4387","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"DSA-4387"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3885-1/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"USN-3885-1"},{"url":"https://github.com/openssh/openssh-portable/commit/6010c0303a422a9c5fa8860c061bf7105eb7f8b2"},{"url":"https://cvsweb.openbsd.org/cgi-bin/cvsweb/src/usr.bin/ssh/scp.c.diff?r1=1.197&r2=1.198&f=h"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20190215-0001/"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/106531","tags":["vdb-entry"],"name":"106531"},{"url":"https://sintonen.fi/advisories/scp-client-multiple-vulnerabilities.txt"},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/201903-16","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"GLSA-201903-16"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2019/03/msg00030.html","tags":["mailing-list"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20190325 [SECURITY] [DLA 1728-1] openssh security update"},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpuapr2019-5072813.html"},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpuoct2019-5072832.html"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2019:3702","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"RHSA-2019:3702"},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/202